# Tier 4: Agent Surface And Scenario Assertions
File: oogrep/qa/tier4_scenarios.oot

Status: ACTIVE. Covers the MCP stdio transport and end-to-end agent scenarios.

## MCP Protocol Assertions

Transport is newline delimited JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout. No socket, no port,
no daemon.

| ID | Frame | Expectation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| T4-P01 | `initialize` | result carries protocolVersion 2024-11-05 |
| T4-P02 | `tools/list` before initialize | JSON-RPC error -32600 |
| T4-P03 | `tools/list` after initialize | declares the `search` tool |
| T4-P04 | `tools/call` name=`search` | result carries content and telemetry |
| T4-P05 | `tools/call` missing pattern | error -32602, never empty success |
| T4-P06 | `tools/call` unknown tool | error -32601 |
| T4-P07 | unknown method | error -32601 |
| T4-P08 | `shutdown` | acknowledged, loop exits at EOF |

## Agent Context Assertions

| ID | Invocation | Expectation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| T4-A01 | `search` with `max_chars` omitted | output capped at 4000 chars |
| T4-A02 | `search` with `max_chars` = 999999 | clamped to 65536 |
| T4-A03 | large result set | `truncated` flag reports honestly |
| T4-A04 | `search` over nonexistent path | error -32602 names the missing path |
| T4-A05 | result text with embedded quotes | escaped, stays valid JSON |

## Invariant Under Test

An agent receives bounded, parseable, honest output. A truncated result must
declare its own truncation rather than present a partial answer as complete.
